# Auto-instantiate the second (base) accelerometer at boot.
#
# This board's ACPI tables only auto-enumerate the display accelerometer
# (ACPI companion MDA6655:00, on i2c-1, appearing as iio:device0). The base
# accelerometer on i2c-3 needs manual instantiation via the i2c `new_device`
# sysfs mechanism (see scripts/add-second-accelerometer.sh); this rule
# triggers that automatically the moment the display accelerometer is
# enumerated by the kernel, so it survives reboot without a manual step.
#
# The i2c bus numbers here (i2c-1 display, i2c-3 base) are specific to the
# U300 variant this repo documents -- confirmed via scripts/dump-dsdt.sh and
# direct sysfs tracing, see README's "I2C bus mapping" notes. Community
# projects targeting older N100/N150 units use i2c-0/i2c-1 instead. Do not
# install this rule as-is without confirming your own unit's mapping first.
#
# Deliberately does NOT set ACCEL_MOUNT_MATRIX (not yet determined on this
# board, see README Status) or ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS} (no daemon service exists
# yet). Both are left for a follow-up once those pieces land.

SUBSYSTEM=="iio", KERNEL=="iio*", SUBSYSTEMS=="i2c", \
        DEVPATH=="*/i2c-1/i2c-MDA6655:00/iio:device0", \
        RUN+="/bin/sh -c 'echo mxc4005 0x15 > /sys/bus/i2c/devices/i2c-3/new_device'"
